        "text": "Page: Thug Mentality 1999. Sentence: Thug Mentality 1999 is the debut solo album by American rapper Krayzie Bone.\nPage: Thug Mentality 1999. Sentence: The double-disc album featured a large selection of guest appearances, including Bone Thugs-n-Harmony, Mariah Carey, The Marley Brothers, Big Pun, Fat Joe, Cuban Link, Gangsta Boo, E-40, 8 Ball & MJG, Kurupt, Treach and Snoop Dogg.\nPage: Gangsta Boo. Sentence: Lola Mitchell (born August 7, 1979), better known as her stage name Gangsta Boo or Lady Boo, is an American rapper from Memphis, Tennessee.\nPage: Uni5 the Prequel: The Untold Story. Sentence: Is an album by Bone Thugs-N-Harmony that features cuts and songs from other releases such as , Strength & Loyalty and Krayzie Bones Thug Mentality 1999.",
